            "created_at": "2025-07-21T13:50:55.256907+00:00",
            "notes": "### \u26a1Powers:\n\n- [Legendary Loadout](item_81067d34-38fb-4057-9336-f387f75dfd5f) to start, as it will be the core of the build thanks to the damage it outputs in a shorter burst than your previous Micro Missiles. \n\n- While there's the added benefit of you being able to hit multiple targets with one barrage, the AOE damage is dramatically increased against you, so be cautious when taking very close fights (i.e.  [Reinhardt](hero_a3b6ca2c-6cbd-43dc-bb78-a728e42fba49) Rocket Hammer swing distance).\n\n### \ud83d\udcab Items:\n\n- [Power Playbook](item_6d8803cf-baa7-46ee-af91-51e7f2301418) is priority, though the rest of the items are really just up to you since it's only Round 1. \n\n- [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) & [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf) are, in my opinion, the best options in the event that you need to kill an opponent faster.\n\n### \u2694\ufe0f Playstyles & Notes:\n\n- As mentioned in the Build Notes, you should opt to take space by going past the enemy tank and eliminate a squishy as fast as possible.\n\n- Take high grounds for easier hits with Micro Missiles and play near safe Health Packs to not stress your Supports. \n\n- Should you be facing a character such as [Reinhardt](hero_a3b6ca2c-6cbd-43dc-bb78-a728e42fba49), [Junker Queen](hero_4794d288-27d9-49e0-a1dd-ffe0f4de3ab1), [Reaper](hero_0449752f-1c58-487b-b9a0-ca727d784457), or other characters that are attacking your teammates up close (and personal), you may want to consider diving them if they can kill your teammates faster than you can kill theirs. You can then time a proper counter-dive once the diving opponent makes their escape, granted if you still have Micro Missiles to use on your opponent.",
