            "created_at": "2025-07-21T13:50:55.256907+00:00",
            "notes": "### \u26a1\ufe0fPowers:\n\n- [Party Protector](item_1ef9061d-cfa4-4f4e-a262-ab1012438e69) should now be your final item, as it can act similarly to a Sound Barrier (Ultimate ability) provided by [Lucio](hero_b38c5d54-a585-4545-b0b8-4d4b205b3768). Note: Characters gain the overhealth mentioned in the power upon activation of the ability, not the explosion.\n\n- [Express Detonation](item_8da4cbad-78cb-4ebd-8bc4-8dc150afec95) is also a good option to consider for unexpected surprises for your enemies to find.\n\n### \ud83d\udcab Items:\n\n- [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) should now be taken because those pesky enemy supports are an absolute nuisance with their healing on your victims at this point.\n\n- Grab other [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) increasing items for even more guarantee on your kills like [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6) or [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56). This should be considered whether you hit the money goal or not, in addition to getting the recommended items.\n\n- If you have a LOT of money, I recommend using the last two slots that are marked as Rare with both [Onslaught Ordinance](item_aa2a5d6d-0f8f-4b27-a44e-331832ec11fa) and [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98), as 95% [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) should be a good threshold to hit considering you would then have a 25% [Cooldown Reduction](stat_cooldown_reduction).\n\n- If you've been taking too much damage, I would recommend [Ogundimu Reduction Field](item_b12daf48-069b-44c1-88fe-221cbcff664d) with [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) to keep you sustained.\n\n### \u2694\ufe0f Playstyles & Notes:\n\n- Now that you've made it to Round 7, I'm gonna need you to breathe and center yourself. \n\n- Remember your goal: Take the high ground and rain missiles from there. Scout out a target and boost in. Be extra reckless if you have Self-Destruct to use as an escape option.\n\n\nCongrats and many thanks for reading this far. I sincerely hope you enjoy using this build as much as I have. The build will be constantly updated for the sake of clarity and if any patches potentially change the playstyle.\n\n**Final note**: A lot of people will call this build dumb, and most of the time it's going to be the opponent. Just be sure to stay humble, to a playstyle that helps you or your team, and most importantly, to have fun.",
